              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for to set sail, then the Latin for a ferryman."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: appellō, appellere",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "appellō, appellere — \"to put in (to land), to bring a ship to shore\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nautae nāvem ad lītus appellunt. The sailors bring the ship in to the shore."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "appellō, appellere, appulī, appulsum, third conjugation. Do not mix it up with appellō, appellāre 'to call', a different verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "appellō, appellere is built from ad- 'to' and pellō 'to drive, to push' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): to drive a ship to land."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
