              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ēgredior, ēgredī — \"to step out, to go out; to land, to disembark\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Viātōrēs ē nāve ēgrediuntur et ad caupōnam ambulant. The travellers get off the ship and walk to the inn."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: ēgredior, ēgredī, ēgressus sum. Ē nāve ēgredī, to disembark. English egress comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ēgredior is built from ē(x)- 'out' and gradior 'to step' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English egress comes from its participle ēgressus."
            }
          ]
        },
