              "text": "nāvigābilis, nāvigābile — \"navigable\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Flūmen magnum et altum est, itaque nāvigābile. The river is big and deep, and so it is navigable."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An adjective of two endings, from nāvigō 'to sail' with -bilis 'that can be'. English navigable comes from it."
            }
